# CODEOWNERS — who GitHub automatically requests a review from on a pull request.
#
# WHY A SINGLE CONCRETE USER AND NOT A TEAM
# The rsync-ai organisation currently has NO teams (`gh api orgs/rsync-ai/teams`
# returns `[]`). A CODEOWNERS line naming a team that does not exist — or a user
# without write access — is a SILENT no-op: GitHub requests no review, blocks
# nothing, and reports no error anywhere. Only add `@rsync-ai/<team>` entries
# after the team exists AND has write access to this repository.
#
# WHY THE SPECIFIC RULES LOOK REDUNDANT TODAY
# Every rule below names the same owner as the global `*` rule, so today they
# change no behaviour. They are here so that the moment a second maintainer or a
# team is added to `*`, review on the security-sensitive trees does not silently
# widen with it — the narrow rules keep it pinned. Update them together.
#
# SYNTAX: .gitignore-style patterns. The LAST matching line wins, so the global
# rule must stay first. A trailing `/` matches the whole subtree.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Global — everything not claimed by a more specific rule below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                                   @rahulv8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authentication, sessions, OAuth, CSRF, RBAC, tenant isolation.
# A regression here is an account-takeover or a cross-workspace data leak.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/api-gateway/internal/handlers/auth*.go             @rahulv8
/api-gateway/internal/handlers/oauth*.go            @rahulv8
/api-gateway/internal/handlers/*_middleware.go      @rahulv8
/api-gateway/internal/security/                     @rahulv8
/backend-orchestrator/internal/security/            @rahulv8

# Credential encryption at rest and session-token hashing. Changing the key
# derivation or the token format is a one-way door for already-stored data.
/shared/go/crypto/                                  @rahulv8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Change data capture and the self-healing agents.
# CDC provisioning order (publication before replication slot) and the healer's
# error classification both cause SILENT data loss when they are got wrong.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/backend-orchestrator/internal/cdc/                 @rahulv8
/backend-orchestrator/internal/agents/sentinel/     @rahulv8
/backend-orchestrator/internal/agents/heal/         @rahulv8
/backend-orchestrator/internal/agents/healer/       @rahulv8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI and supply chain. These run on self-hosted runners and hold release
# credentials, so a workflow edit is a privileged change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/workflows/                                 @rahulv8
/.github/dependabot.yml                             @rahulv8
/CODEOWNERS                                         @rahulv8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment artifacts users run in their own clusters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/deploy/helm/                                       @rahulv8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Licensing and security policy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/LICENSE                                            @rahulv8
/DCO                                                @rahulv8
/SECURITY.md                                        @rahulv8
